' Daily run overview; nine participants represent the timer, script, four CLI steps, sources, database and configured API.
@startuml
title Daily run (9 participants)
hide footbox
participant "Timer + daily service" as Timer
participant "daily.sh" as Daily
participant "CLI run" as Run
participant "Sources + laptop import" as Sources
database Postgres as DB
participant "CLI match" as Match
participant "Configured API\nTokenRouter if configured" as Router
participant "CLI analyze" as Analyze
participant "CLI health" as Health

Timer -> Daily : 07:00 Europe/Tirane
Daily -> Run : run
Run -> Sources : fetch named sources, then registered ATS boards
Sources --> Run : postings or errors
Run -> DB : merge / save postings, discover ATS slugs, record outcomes
Daily -> Match : match
Match -> DB : load profile and postings
Match -> Router : embed missing / different-model vectors
Router --> Match : vectors
Match -> DB : cache vectors, rank, set queue flags
Daily -> Analyze : analyze
Analyze -> DB : queued jobs without current-model analysis
Analyze -> Router : job facts + whole-profile fit
Router --> Analyze : JSON facts, evidence, explanation
Analyze -> DB : save validated analysis and explanation
Daily -> Health : health
Health -> DB : latest runs + seven-day yield medians
Health --> Daily : report source problems
Daily --> Timer : fail if any command failed

legend bottom
  All four steps run even after an earlier failure.
  Queue: percentile >= 97 AND similarity >= 0.55.
  Embedding / analysis calls retry once on supported failures.
  Cached vectors and analysis are reused by model.
endlegend
@enduml
